# world_r5.probe — P3/R5 (PLAN-RENDER): capsule-SDF wall strokes through the real
# pipeline (worldmesh::build_wall_mesh → view's wall shader), same scene as
# world_r4 (src/worldprobe.loft, seed 1337 surface). Expected values are the
# BLUEPRINT's numbers (tools/blueprints/wall_sdf.py) confirmed live 2026-06-12:
#   stroke interior = uColor (0.92,0.82,0.45) -> (235,209,115) at vis 1.0
#   remembered stroke = x0.451 (the manufactured block on the nearest wall) -> (106,94,52)
#   cross-stroke ramp: solid interior -> ~1px AA -> background, monotonic
# Deterministic scene: pinned pixels are stable for THIS worldprobe code.
#
# ── RE-AIMED 2026-08-11, AND THE EXPECTED VALUES ARE UNTOUCHED ──────────────────────────
# The three pins above were measured on the June town wall. Plan #17 then CUT GATES in that
# wall and posted a guard on the works, so the wall moved and the old coordinates sat on
# open ground — every one of them read lit grass (165,175,114).
#
# ⚠ THE FRAME WAS NOT ADOPTED AS GOLDEN. Each colour below is still the blueprint's number,
# byte for byte; only WHERE the feature is has changed, which is the one thing a re-cut wall
# is entitled to change. The proof that the contract itself never moved is in world_r4:
# `rem_grass` passes at its ORIGINAL June coordinate at dmax=0 once the scene bug is fixed.
# Each new pin is the most uniform pixel of its feature in the frame (stroke_interior: 5x5
# uniform; rem_stroke: 3x3, which is as thick as a dimmed one-hex stroke gets), so a
# sub-pixel camera nudge cannot flip it.

image /tmp/probe_world.png

probe stroke_interior 785 169 235 209 115 tol 4
probe rem_stroke 633 581 106 94 52 tol 4
ramp stroke_edge 761 200 761 206 dec samples 7 tol 2
